## Approach

Add a Dart `package:` URI → workspace-relative file path resolver that runs as a post-parse step, populating the existing `imports.resolved_file_id` column. This is the single missing link — all downstream consumers (DD constraints, guard, PageRank, sutra_deps) already query `import_edges()` which reads `resolved_file_id`. No changes needed downstream.

The resolver builds a package map by walking workspace `pubspec.yaml` files at parse time. This is cheap even on large monorepos (tens of pubspecs, each ~1KB, read once per parse cycle). Lazy — built only when Dart files are present.

Also handle relative imports (`import '../foo.dart'`, `import 'bar.dart'`) which have the same resolution gap.

