### Step 6: Path normalization for relative imports

`resolve_relative_import` needs to handle `../` and `./` in paths. Use `std::path::Path` join + a simple normalization (iteratively resolve `.` and `..` components). Don't use `canonicalize()` — it resolves symlinks and requires the file to exist; we just need logical path normalization.

```rust
fn normalize_path(path: &Path) -> Option<String> {
    let mut components = Vec::new();
    for c in path.components() {
        match c {
            Component::ParentDir => { components.pop(); }
            Component::CurDir => {}
            Component::Normal(s) => { components.push(s); }
            _ => return None, // prefix/root — shouldn't appear
        }
    }
    Some(components.iter().map(|c| c.to_str().unwrap_or("")).collect::<Vec<_>>().join("/"))
}
```

